{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Vision Transformer Encoder Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MultiHeadSelfAttention`, with `qkv` and output projections, the scaled-dot-product attention math, and shape assertions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `FeedForward`, the 4x-expansion GELU MLP."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Block`, a pre-LN block composing attention and feed-forward sub-layers with residuals."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `ViT`, a stack of 12 blocks with a final LayerNorm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `VisionEncoder`, which wires `VisionFrontEnd` from lesson 58 to the `ViT` stack and exposes a `forward()` returning the contextual sequence and the pooled CLS vector."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that runs a synthesized 224x224 fixture image through the full encoder and prints input shape, output shape, parameter count, and the CLS norm at every other layer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: the fixture is encoded to a `(1, 197, 768)` tensor. The CLS norm drifts upward as the layers compose, then stabilizes at the final LayerNorm. Total parameters report at about 86M."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add register tokens (4 learned vectors prepended after CLS) and rerun. Compare attention map smoothness via the entropy of the softmax distribution on the last layer.\n\n2. Swap pre-LN for post-LN and train for one epoch on a synthetic shape classifier. Observe which one trains stably without LR warm-up.\n\n3. Implement causal masking as an `attn_mask` argument so the same block can be reused as a decoder block. The mask shape is `(seq, seq)`, lower-triangular.\n\n4. Profile a forward pass at batch sizes 1, 8, 64 with `torch.profiler`. The MLP layer dominates wall time, not attention.\n\n5. Replace one attention head's q-k-v projections with a low-rank LoRA adapter, freeze the rest, and verify the gradient only flows where you expect."
      ]
    }
  ],
